A TextField(value:format:) shows the binding's formatted value on every recomposition, so "7." can't be typed and an emptied field refills; a field created with formatsValue keeps the typed text while it has focus, shows a value changed from outside the field, and when focus leaves (submit included) shows the formatted value and writes it back, as SwiftUI on iOS does, so a field cleared and left shows the value it still holds. skip-fuse-ui 0005 passes the flag. Proposed upstream.

